# seed.ll is a generated compiler artifact (machine-emitted LLVM IR,
# ~500k lines, version-locked to the source that produced it). Text
# diffs are noise and text merges are always wrong — the only correct
# conflict resolution is to pick one side as a bootstrap stepping
# stone and regenerate from the merged source (make update-seed).
# See bootstrap/docs/SEED_MERGES.md.
bootstrap/seed/seed.ll -diff merge=binary

# Since the pin-don't-vendor migration seed.ll is fetched per
# seed/seed.lock and no longer
# tracked; the entry above still protects pre-lock history during
# merges/rebases. seed.lock conflicts mean two seed-train advances
# raced: artifacts are immutable and content-pinned, so resolution is
# mechanical — take the HIGHER version line (diagnose.sh --seed-merge
# automates the full regenerate path when the union needs restaging).
